        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T19:28:05Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): comment the setup, operation and tool in posted programs\n\nEvery built-in post now writes, in its own comment syntax, the setup\nname where its first section opens, each operation's name, kind and\nwork offset at its preamble, and each tool's number, name, kind,\ndiameter and corner radius just ahead of its tool call. Only comment\nlines are added; no motion changes.\n\npost::dump carries four new optional PARAMs for this (OperationKind,\nSetupName, ToolKind, ToolCornerRadius), each written only when stated,\nso legacy streams and user scripts read as before. User text is cleaned\nper dialect: ASCII only, capped at 40 characters, and ( ) % ; (plus *\non Heidenhain) never reach a comment.\n\nRefs #257\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
